From: enij90 <226572015+enij90@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: nt36523: declare a VRR range on the kirby BOE panel

The Lenovo TB321FU kirby panels (CSOT and BOE) support dynamic refresh
through VFP extension, as the stock firmware dfps_immediate_porch_mode_vfp
mode down to 30 Hz confirms.  Declare a VRR-capable monitor range so the
DPU AVR block (patch 0107) can hold the vertical front porch between
commits instead of scanning out repeated frames at the fixed refresh rate.

The floor is set to 40 Hz: low enough to cover 30-fps game output with
margin, high enough to keep the maximum frame period (25 ms) comfortable.

Only the BOE panel is declared VRR-capable. Enabling it on the CSOT
panel made the display glitch and become unresponsive (issue #5), and
we have no CSOT unit to characterize its VFP tolerance, so the CSOT
panel stays at a fixed refresh until it can be tested on hardware.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-novatek-nt36523.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-novatek-nt36523.c
@@ -82,6 +82,7 @@
 	bool has_dcs_backlight;
 	bool has_dsc;
 	bool display_on_after_dsc;
+	unsigned int vrr_min_hz;
 };
 
 static inline struct panel_info *to_panel_info(struct drm_panel *panel)
@@ -1502,6 +1504,7 @@
 	.is_dual_dsi = true,
 	.has_dsc = true,
 	.display_on_after_dsc = true,	/* reuses kirby_csot_display_on_sequence (identical) */
+	.vrr_min_hz = 40,
 };
 
 static const struct panel_desc j606f_boe_desc = {
@@ -1727,6 +1730,20 @@
 	connector->display_info.width_mm = pinfo->desc->width_mm;
 	connector->display_info.height_mm = pinfo->desc->height_mm;
 	connector->display_info.bpc = pinfo->desc->bpc;
+	if (pinfo->desc->vrr_min_hz) {
+		unsigned int max_hz = 0;
+
+		for (i = 0; i < pinfo->desc->num_modes; i++) {
+			const struct drm_display_mode *m = &pinfo->desc->modes[i];
+
+			max_hz = max_t(unsigned int, max_hz,
+				       DIV_ROUND_UP(m->clock * 1000,
+						    m->htotal * m->vtotal));
+		}
+		connector->display_info.monitor_range.min_vfreq = pinfo->desc->vrr_min_hz;
+		connector->display_info.monitor_range.max_vfreq = max_hz;
+		drm_connector_set_vrr_capable_property(connector, true);
+	}
 
 	return pinfo->desc->num_modes;
 }
